= Problem
Artemis currently does not provide dedicated support for presentations as part of its assessment workflow. Instructors therefore often use spreadsheets, personal notes, or other external tools to organize presentations and document assessment results. These disconnected workflows separate presentation-related information from the actual course environment and increase the overall organizational effort for instructors and tutors.

Instructors currently need to define assessment criteria manually, document the results, and transfer grades themselves. This not only increases the organizational effort and makes the process more prone to mistakes. Tutors involved in the assessment process may also use different criteria or different interpretations of grading standards, which reduces transparency and consistency for students. Different presentation contexts further increase the complexity of the problem. Some presentations are directly linked to exercises, for example when students present a project submission. Other presentations are independent assessment components, such as seminar talks.